// The sun's shadows, cached (REBUILD-PLAN §6.3, review M1).
//
// Before: every frame the whole shadow map (4096², 2048² on a phone) was cleared and every caster
// near you drawn into it again (300-570 draws, ~1.5 ms of the main thread on a desktop, a quarter
// of a phone's frame), for a sun that never moves and things that almost never do.
//
// Now:
//   - the things that never move are drawn once into a STATIC map, over a box a little bigger than
//     before (±half m instead of ±24 m), re-centred only after you have walked `recentre` m from
//     its centre (snapped to whole shadow texels, so shadows never crawl), at most every MIN_GAP s
//     unless you would otherwise leave the ±24 m you always had;
//   - things that move get their real shadow every frame on top (the "overlay", high/ultra and
//     mid): the few small patches of the map where they were and are are copied back from a copy
//     of the still map (colour and depth, a GPU copy) and only the movers are drawn again. Without
//     the overlay (low) movers don't cast into the map; characters and rides get a soft blob
//     instead (island.js);
//   - the still map is drawn straight into the map the picture uses, at full size, then copied into
//     that copy, which may be smaller (D-E1c: half size on high, 32 MB instead of 128 MB; full size
//     on ultra and mid): only the patches round the movers come back from it, a little coarser;
//   - what moves is found out, not listed by hand: every caster drawn into the static map is
//     watched (its world matrix) and the moment one moves it becomes a mover. The player, the other
//     player and the rides are movers from the start.
//
// When the static map is redrawn (every trigger, so nothing ever stays stale):
//   1. the box is re-centred (you walked far enough), or you'd leave the ±24 m you always had;
//   2. the sun's direction changed (theme, day/night, weather): island.js calls invalidate();
//   3. something drawn into it moved (it becomes a mover), turned invisible, or stopped/started
//      casting;
//   4. something hidden near you became visible (a room's insides or far-off details drawn again by
//      distance, the halloween/christmas sets, the lookout's roof): the hidden groups that hold
//      casters are watched;
//   5. a shadow-casting thing was added to or taken out of the world (a room furnished, a
//      decoration hung on the willow, a zone streamed in);
//   6. the map's size changed (the adaptive step in the loop) or the graphics came back after
//      being taken away;
//   7. a slow safety refresh (SAFETY s), so anything missed above heals by itself.
